.TH PAINT 1 "2026-08-06" "paint" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
paint \- a simple, easy-to-use image editor
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B paint
.RI [ FILE ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B paint
is a raster image editor for the Linux desktop, in the spirit of the classic
Windows accessory. It offers pencil, brush, eraser, fill, shape and text tools,
rectangular and free-form selection, the usual flip, rotate, resize, canvas
size and skew operations, deep undo, drag-and-drop and clipboard support.
.PP
If
.I FILE
is given and names an image the editor can read, it is opened on start-up.
Otherwise a blank canvas is created at the size last used.
.SH FORMATS
Reads and writes PNG, JPEG, BMP, GIF, TIFF, TGA and ICO.
Reads WebP, Photoshop (flattened) and Netpbm.
.SH KEYBOARD
.TP
.B Ctrl+N, Ctrl+O, Ctrl+S, Ctrl+Shift+S
New, Open, Save, Save As
.TP
.B Ctrl+Z, Ctrl+Y
Undo, Redo
.TP
.B Ctrl+X, Ctrl+C, Ctrl+V
Cut, Copy, Paste
.TP
.B Ctrl+A, Ctrl+Shift+A
Select All, Deselect
.TP
.B Ctrl+plus, Ctrl+minus, Ctrl+0, Ctrl+9
Zoom in, Zoom out, Actual size, Fit to window
.TP
.B Ctrl+scroll
Zoom around the pointer
.TP
.B Escape
Cancel the current gesture, or drop the selection
.PP
Single letters select tools: P pencil, B brush, E eraser, F fill, K colour
picker, T text, L line, C curve, R rectangle, D rounded rectangle, O ellipse,
G polygon, S rectangular selection, A free-form selection.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/io.github.rbuache.paint/shared_preferences.json
Theme choice, recent files, default canvas size and custom colours. Removing
this file resets the application to its defaults. It is not owned by the
package, so uninstalling leaves it in place.
.SH BUGS
Report issues at https://github.com/rbuache/paint/issues
